<p>Mexican special forces arrested Audias Flores Silva, known as “El Jardinero,” in Nayarit on Monday in a Navy-led operation targeting a senior Jalisco New Generation Cartel commander whom officials identified as a possible successor to Nemesio Oseguera, “El Mencho,” following Oseguera’s death in February. Security Minister Omar García Harfuch said Flores had an arrest warrant in Mexico and was sought by U.S. authorities for extradition; the United States had offered a $5 million reward for information leading to his capture. The Navy said the arrest followed an extended surveillance effort that used intelligence from U.S. agencies. Officials said forces located Flores near El Mirador, north of Puerto Vallarta, after members of his security ring scattered during the operation. Mexican authorities later announced the arrest of César Alejandro “N,” known as “El Güero Conta,” whom they described as tied to Flores&#x27; financial network and the cartel.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/0NssFyxRqgAOMq6NnJqx1VPZAh_G0SfzouEYP4w-E0RKHKnN9YhZdBpNmR8nRu1_5zqiPte4JfSiORMxlhf6shRX1eXUjEmqoseesRaxkyaq07BfwtHJg_ASdULHiOJOBbexf3WVA_e17VQBLfbBdLQJknbxn5Wxt6fLPJvDNa6zgpqgECnGBLzxYDe8AQ8wnn1biD_dLY5jp8pUELFVHrvTVmVf57E7bJzU5cYaU66z51ms1AvJPACNmnT7AnSBEi_Ea48cn8BfaIEx' alt='Members of Mexican Special Forces escort Audias Flores, known as “El Jardinero,” in Nayarit, Mexico, in a handout distributed on April 27, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Cartel role: Mexican authorities and security analysts linked Flores to CJNG operations in Nayarit, Jalisco, Zacatecas and other western states, including methamphetamine laboratories and U.S.-bound trafficking routes.</li><li>U.S. case: U.S. authorities accused Flores of drug-trafficking offenses, including conspiracy to distribute at least five kilograms of cocaine and at least one kilogram of heroin for importation into the United States.</li><li>Financial arrest: García Harfuch said César Alejandro “N” was accused of laundering illegal proceeds through companies and front people, including purchases of aircraft, boats, houses and ranches.</li><li>Operational scale: The Navy said more than 500 troops, six helicopters and other aircraft took part in the final operation near a cabin guarded by about 30 pickup trucks and more than 60 gunmen.</li></ul><blockquote>The operation was carried out with surgical precision without a single shot being fired - Mexican Navy</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>El País: The newspaper described the capture as a success for Mexico&#x27;s Navy, noting that the force had recently faced criticism over fuel-smuggling scandals and an interoceanic train accident. (<a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-04-28/mexico-deals-second-major-blow-to-jalisco-new-generation-cartel-in-just-two-months.html'>El País</a>)</li><li>President Claudia Sheinbaum: Sheinbaum called the two arrests “very relevant” and said they reflected progress in intelligence and investigative work by Mexican security institutions. (<a href='https://noticiassin.com/mundo/2026/04/28/sheinbaum-destaca-golpes-al-cjng-tras-captura-de-el-1987978/'>Noticias SIN</a>)</li><li>David Saucedo, security specialist: Saucedo described Flores as El Mencho&#x27;s “right-hand man” and said he had negotiated an alliance between CJNG and Los Chapitos on Oseguera&#x27;s behalf. (<a href='https://www.teletica.com/internacional/mexico-captura-a-presunto-sucesor-de-el-mencho-en-gran-operativo_407731'>Teletica</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-mexico-jalisco-cartel-leader-capture/'>Mexico captures top Jalisco leader ‘El Jardinero’ in another blow to the cartel</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/mexicos-military-captures-top-cartel-leader-in-another-blow-to-the-jalisco-new-generation-cartel/article70917786.ece'>Mexico&#x27;s military captures top cartel leader in another blow to the Jalisc